## Instructions

### 1. Understand the Codebase

Before making changes, review:

- `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` — the dependency rule and platform seams
- `AGENTS.md` — agent instructions and conventions
- `CLAUDE.md` — Claude-specific instructions
- `README.md` — project overview and build commands

The one rule:

> **Ported, not branched.** Platform differences are absorbed by a portable
> interface, never by `#ifdef` in the code that consumes it.

### 2. Build the Project

```bash
# Windows
scripts\build.bat

# Or manually (any platform)
cmake -S . -B build
cmake --build build --config Release
```

### 3. Run Tests

```bash
ctest --test-dir build -C Release --output-on-failure
```

All 107 tests must pass before your changes are complete.

### 4. Implement Changes

Follow the architecture:

| Layer | Directory | Rules |
|-------|-----------|-------|
| Entry | `src/app/`, `src/ui/`, `src/cli/` | Only outbound calls |
| Domain | `src/markdown/`, `src/filesystem/` | Business logic |
| Core | `src/terminal/`, `src/utils/` | High fan-in, foundational |
| Platform | `src/platform/` | Only `#ifdef` allowed here |

### 5. Verify

```bash
ctest --test-dir build -C Release --output-on-failure
```

Zero failures required.

## Constraints

### Must Do

- Follow the dependency rule (no `#ifdef` above `src/platform/`)
- Use `std::filesystem::path` for all path operations
- Use `std::getenv` not `_dupenv_s`, `std::fopen` not `fopen_s`
- Run tests after every change
- Check neighboring files for style consistency

### Must Not Do

- Add `#ifdef` in UI, parser, renderer, or app code
- Include `windows.h` outside `src/platform/windows/`
- Add third-party dependencies
- Use MSVC-only secure CRT functions
- Concatenate path separators manually (`"\\"` or `"/"`)
- Use `uninsdeletevalue` for PATH in Inno Setup installer

## Code Style

- C++20 with `CXX_EXTENSIONS OFF`
- MSVC: `/W4 /permissive- /utf-8 /Zc:__cplusplus /EHsc`
- GCC/Clang: `-Wall -Wextra -Wpedantic`
- No comments unless requested
- No emojis unless requested

